OL,3,GNEWSAHow to watch the partial lunar
OL,4,Aeclipse from Northern Ireland
OL,5,
OL,6,FStargazers have the chance to see a
OL,7,Fstunning partial lunar eclipse early on
OL,8,FFriday morning, as the moon enters
OL,9,FEarth's shadow.
OL,11,FAt its peak, roughly 93% of the Moon's
OL,12,Fdiameter will be covered, making the
OL,13,Fevent look close to a total eclipse.
OL,15,FFor people in Northern Ireland hoping
OL,16,Fto catch a glimpse, the biggest
OL,17,Fchallenge will be the early start,
OL,18,Fpossible cloud cover, and the Moon's
OL,19,Flow position in the western sky.
OL,21,FMore than 90% of the Moon will be
OL,22,Feclipsed shortly after 5am.
OL,23,APub: 27-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
